s":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":19,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I did not change any code for PKT-0057. The two files the packet lets me touch can't hold a fix that keeps the \"no missing glyphs after a remote change\" rule, so I recorded a follow-up request with the right files instead.\n\n**Where the walk comes from:** each time remote changes are applied, the code goes through `pre_Save` (`word/api.js` ~8560), then `CheckFontNeeds` (`word/Drawing/DrawingDocument.js` ~6512), then `CDocument.Document_Get_AllFontNames`, which walks every paragraph and calls `ParaRun.Get_AllFontNames`. That last function (`word/Editor/Run.js` ~3125) loops over every item in every run, and that loop is where the time goes. The list of changed objects is cleared during the apply step (`Apply_OtherChanges`), before `pre_Save` runs.\n\n**Why I stopped:**\n- The call site (`api.js`, `DrawingDocument.js`), the expensive loop (`Run.js`) and the changed-object list (`CollaborativeEditing.js`) are all outside the packet's target.\n- From `Document.js` and `Paragraph.js` alone there is no reliable way to know which paragraphs or runs a remote change touched. A font change on a run does not notify its paragraph, so a cache there could skip fonts.\n\n**What I did:**\n- Wrote a follow-up request in `.theseus/spawn/PKT-0057-incremental-font-name-collection-for-remote-chan.md`. It targets `api.js`, `DrawingDocument.js`, `CollaborativeEditing.js`, `Run.js` and `Document.js`, carries the same contract and acceptance command, and lists the call chain above. The plan is to record the changed objects while changes are applied, then collect fonts only from those after a remote change, keeping the full walk when a document opens.\n- Filled in the Executor log, Spawned packets and Lessons sections of the packet, added the friction line, and committed (`a705335`).\n- No before/after profile: with no code change there is nothing to measure, and I did not use the Document Server.\n\n**Checks:** `bash .theseus/oracle/unit.sh` gave 178 passed, 1 skipped. `theseus validate` reported 0 errors and 1 warning, which I didn't look into.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas (sdkjs-word):** applying remote changes reloads fonts by walking the whole document through `pre_Save` and `CheckFontNeeds`. The changed objects are only available during `Apply_OtherChanges`. Packets should choose their target files after tracing the call chain, not from the profiler's list of slow functions.","ttft_ms":1884,"type":"result","duration_ms":83071,"uuid":"6bd7e057-ee1b-4175-9c65-105bde5794ce","ttft_stream_ms":948,"time_to_request_ms":371,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":214,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":27,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":9,"engine_pickup":8,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":15,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":14,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":28,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":5,"request_build":10},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":162,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":178,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":234,"process_anon_mib_result":142,"process_peak_rss_mib":273,"process_cpu_ms_turn":3202,"process_wall_ms_turn":83071,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1394,"process_wall_ms_streaming":53943,"main_stream_count":19,"main_stream_event_count":922,"main_stream_chunk_count":565,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":15,"cpu_ms":23,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":8,"ambient_wait_ms":14,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":948,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":18984621,"warm_spare_claimed":false